    fix(bound-port-truth-1): ensure_bind() timeout fallback prefers the real bound port
    
    ensure_bind()'s 2s readiness-poll timeout previously fell back to the
    configured (cfg.server.host, cfg.server.port) unconditionally, which can
    differ from the daemon's real bound port when bind_with_retry
    auto-incremented past a taken port. Extract the fallback decision into a
    pure bind_fallback(lock, cfg) helper that prefers daemon::read_lock()'s
    real port -- written by serve() right after bind, before the daemon
    answers its own health check -- and only falls through to the configured
    port when no lock exists at all.

